@nsobid-4B159F0F7A360669738390EE8657B4F0

# ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 - 60 FPS cutscene fix

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Keeps cutscenes and other frame-stepped animation at normal speed at 60 FPS.
//
// Once per frame the game converts elapsed time into a step measured in 30 Hz
// frames (sub_710091DBB0, scale = 30 / 1000 ms). A step under 1.0 is rounded
// up to 1.0 and the difference carried as a debt against the next frame. At
// 30 FPS that only smooths jitter; at 60 FPS every frame measures 0.5, the debt
// saturates, and the step stays pinned at 1.0, so everything using it runs at
// double speed. The rounding floor, the debt base and the value written are
// moved from 1.0 to 0.5, one 60 Hz frame. The 2.0 ceiling stays as the hitch
// guard.
//
// When the engine's fixed-step flag is set the loop skips the measurement and
// writes the step it was passed instead. That argument is loaded once before
// the main loop and is lowered to 0.5 as well.
//
// REQUIRES [60 FPS].

@enabled
// Frame-step quantiser.
0091DC94 01102C1E   // FMOV S1,#0.5 (was 1.0) = rounding threshold
0091DCA0 01102C1E   // FMOV S1,#0.5 (was 1.0) = debt base
0091DCAC 08E0A752   // MOVZ W8,#0x3F00,LSL#16 = 0.5f (was 1.0f) = rounded step
// Fixed step passed in by the main loop.
003E397C 08102C1E   // FMOV S8,#0.5 (was 1.0)
@stop

// Frame-step fix by MrComputerRevo
// (https://gbatemp.net/threads/astral-chain-rom-hacking-bible.547050/post-8777070)
// and masagrator (https://github.com/masagrator), packaged by StevensND
// (https://github.com/StevensND/switch-port-mods). The fixed-step path is
// patched at its argument instead of dropping the store; re-verified against
// 1.0.1 and byte-verified against the IDB.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
